{{!
    @template local_simplemcp/instructions

    Step-by-step guide shown to a learner who wants to connect an MCP client
    to their own account.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * introhtml - Opening paragraph, already-escaped HTML.
    * serverheading - Heading above the server address.
    * serverintro - Sentence introducing the server address.
    * serverurl - The MCP endpoint URL to paste into the client.
    * sections - Array of {heading, bodyhtml} guide sections, already-escaped HTML.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "introhtml": "You can connect ChatGPT or Claude to your account.",
        "serverheading": "Server address",
        "serverintro": "Both apps need this URL when you add the connector:",
        "serverurl": "https://moodle.example.com/local/simplemcp/endpoint.php",
        "sections": [{"heading": "ChatGPT", "bodyhtml": "<ol><li>Open ChatGPT.</li></ol>"}]
    }
}}
<div class="box generalbox local-simplemcp-instructions">
    <p>{{{introhtml}}}</p>

    <h4>{{serverheading}}</h4>
    <p>{{serverintro}}</p>
    <p><code>{{serverurl}}</code></p>

    {{#sections}}
        <h4>{{heading}}</h4>
        {{{bodyhtml}}}
    {{/sections}}
</div>
